  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "One bag contains one blue ball and two red balls. A second bag contains two blue balls and one red ball. A bag is randomly chosen and then a ball is drawn from the bag.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p24-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the probability that the selected ball is blue.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac12$",
          "worked": "Let $A$ denote choosing the first bag and $B$ denote drawing a blue ball. The two bags are equally likely to be chosen.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(B)&=\\Pr(A\\cap B)+\\Pr(A'\\cap B)\\\\\\Pr(B)&=\\frac12\\times\\frac13+\\frac12\\times\\frac23\\\\\\Pr(B)&=\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p24-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the probability that the first bag was chosen given that the selected ball is blue.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac13$\n\nDivide the probability of choosing the first bag and drawing blue by the total probability of drawing blue.",
          "worked": "Let $A$ denote choosing the first bag and $B$ denote drawing a blue ball. From part (a), $\\Pr(B)=\\frac12$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(A\\cap B)&=\\frac12\\times\\frac13\\\\\\Pr(A\\cap B)&=\\frac16\\\\\\Pr(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{\\Pr(A\\cap B)}{\\Pr(B)}\\\\\\Pr(A\\mid B)&=\\frac{\\frac16}{\\frac12}\\\\\\Pr(A\\mid B)&=\\frac13.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
